{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And may Elohim give you.</b> The vav of 'וְיִתֶּן' is superfluous, and the Sages interpreted it (Genesis Rabbah 66:3): He gives and gives again. And the explanation of the matter is thus: for it is known that in all the commandments a person performs, they are not sufficient to repay, 'as recompense for benefits already rendered' (Isaiah 59:18), those goodnesses that the Holy One, blessed be He, has already done for him from the day of his birth; and whatever a person does of the commandments he does by way of payment. And in all the goodnesses we receive from Him, blessed be He, His kindness prevails over us, and the Holy One, blessed be He, anticipates with His goodnesses in every giving, as it is written (Psalms 59:11), 'My El of kindness will anticipate me'; and it is written (Psalms 21:4), 'For You anticipate him with blessings of good'; and it is written (Job 41:3), 'Who has anticipated Me that I should pay him?' Now according to this reasoning: if a person should have a worthless thought, saying, 'Behold, the past is gone, and what profit is it that we serve HaShem? Never will I have a debt upon Him' — you too shall return your words and go out and say to him, 'Go forth and see what the people are doing' — for the custom of merchants who give on credit is that when the buyer pays him the old debt, the merchant then once again gives him goods on credit, and so on forever. But if he does not pay the old debt, he no longer gives him goods. So too the great Merchant on credit — the Holy One, blessed be He, and blessed is His name: when a person pays with his commandments the first credit, the Holy One, blessed be He, gives again on credit. And this is what was said: He gives and gives again." "Another matter: since the Garden of Eden entered with him — and from this Isaac judged that this one who had entered had great reward awaiting him in the spiritual world in the Garden of Eden, for there 'HaShem commanded the blessing, life forever' (Psalms 133:3) — therefore he said 'וְיִתֶּן' with the conjunctive vav, to say that in addition to the spiritual success stored away for you for the World to Come, 'and may He give you' also in this world 'of the dew of the heavens' and so forth (Genesis 27:28), so that you may merit two tables." "And some say that the vav of 'וְיִתֵּן' indicates that a person should not rely on a miracle, but should do what is his, with all that he finds in his power to do, and what nature lacks the miracle will supply, as our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Sifre Re'eh 15, 18): 'One might think even if he sits idle — Scripture says, \"in all that you do.\"' Therefore it says 'וְיִתֵּן,' that is to say: after you have already done all that was in your power to do, then also HaShem will give you from His good storehouse, as it is written (Psalms 85:12–13), 'Truth from the earth will sprout, and righteousness from the heavens will look down; also HaShem will give the good' and so forth. For first you must do your work — in truth, however, indeed, for HaShem will not send His help to one who works works and human contrivances not in righteousness, not in truth, and not in justice; but to one who engages in truth and faithfulness, HaShem will pay His help from the sanctuary. And when human efforts first sprout from the earth, then on the side of kindness HaShem looks down from His heights — and with what does He look down? 'Also HaShem will give the good, and our land will yield its produce.' With the word 'also' He sealed the whole matter, and it is self-evident."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "The phrase פוק חזי מאי עמא דבר ('Go forth and see what the people are doing') is a well-known Talmudic idiom; rendered here literally as it appears.", 1 "I read וי״ו העיטוף as 'conjunctive vav' (the vav that binds to what precedes); the term literally means 'the wrapping/embracing vav.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:30:35.598489695Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}